    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\">Subtypes of T-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma (T-ALL/LBL)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Pei Lin",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 119.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"159\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Subtype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 372.6pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunophenotype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Relative frequency</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 119.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"159\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cortical</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 372.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD1a+, sCD3&minus;, CD4 and CD8&nbsp;double-positive or double-negative</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">60&ndash;75%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 119.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"159\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Medullary (mature)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 372.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD1a&minus;, sCD3+, CD4+ or CD8+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">10&ndash;15%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 119.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"159\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>ETP phenotype<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 372.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"497\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD1a&minus;, CD8&minus;, CD5 weak, with &ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;stem and/or myeloid markers</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">5&ndash;15%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">sCD3, surface CD3; ETP, early T-precursor.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Defined as the expression (&gt;&nbsp;25%) of &ge;&nbsp;1 myeloid or stem cell&ndash;associated marker such as CD34, KIT (CD117), CD13, CD33, CD11b, CD65, or HLA-DR, with negative myeloperoxidase (&lt;&nbsp;3%) and weak CD5 (&lt;&nbsp;75%). Cases with CD5 expression &gt;&nbsp;75% are considered nearly ETP type with absence of CD1a and CD8 (&lt;&nbsp;5%). ETP T-ALL/LBL overlaps with pro&ndash; or pre&ndash;T-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma, described before <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{19147408}</span><span class=\"TableTextChar\">.</span></p>",
